Repair only the supplied scientific or grammatical issues. Return {sections:[{id:number,patches:[{before:string,after:string,issueIndex:number}],reason:string}]}. Include each supplied section exactly once. Use exact unique substrings in its candidate. At most 3 non-overlapping patches per section; their combined BEFORE text must cover at most 35% of that section. issueIndex refers to that section's issues. Keep wording elsewhere unchanged. Restore the original meaning, uncertainty and proposal status. No extra style pass. If bounded repairs cannot solve the issues, return patches:[] and explain.
INPUT DATA:
{"sections": [{"id": 1, "heading": "Introduction", "original": "Readers can easily treat a date placed beside a building description as the date of construction. That inference is not always supported by the sampled material. In this proposal, the association between the charcoal and the building remains uncertain [S1]. Clear writing should make the evidential link explicit instead of relying on the reader to supply a stronger connection.", "candidate": "Readers might mistakenly interpret a date next to a building description as the date of construction. However, this inference is not always supported by the sampled material. In this proposal, the association between the charcoal and the building remains uncertain [S1]. Therefore, clear writing should explicitly make the evidential link, rather than rely on the reader to infer a stronger connection.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "Clear writing should make the evidential link explicit", "revisedQuote": "clear writing should explicitly make the evidential link", "problem": "The revised wording is awkward and can suggest establishing a link rather than clearly stating the evidential relationship and its uncertainty."}]}, {"id": 4, "heading": "Planned Evaluation", "original": "The evaluation will report whether a reader can distinguish material age from event timing and recover the stated interval from each description. We will inspect summaries that select a single date or imply that the fragment securely dates construction. The interval midpoint will not be treated as an established construction date [S2]. These errors will be recorded separately from ordinary stylistic awkwardness.", "candidate": "The evaluation will assess whether readers can distinguish material age from event timing and recover the stated interval from each description. We will examine summaries that select a single date or imply that the fragment securely dates construction. The interval midpoint will not be treated as an established construction date [S2]. These errors will be recorded separately from ordinary stylistic issues.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "The evaluation will report whether a reader can distinguish material age from event timing and recover the stated interval from each description.", "revisedQuote": "The evaluation will assess whether readers can distinguish material age from event timing and recover the stated interval from each description.", "problem": "Assessing reader understanding does not preserve the explicit commitment to report the evaluation findings."}]}, {"id": 5, "heading": "Limitations and Conclusion", "original": "The proposed study concerns the communication of existing evidence, not a new dating analysis. It cannot resolve the uncertain association between the fragment and the building [S1]. A careful synthesis may therefore leave an important historical question open. Its value would lie in making that uncertainty understandable without presenting an interval estimate as a settled event date.", "candidate": "The proposed study focuses on the communication of existing evidence, rather than conducting a new dating analysis. It cannot resolve the uncertain association between the charcoal fragment and the building [S1]. A careful synthesis may therefore leave an important historical question open. Its value lies in making this uncertainty understandable without presenting the interval estimate as a settled event date.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "Its value would lie in making that uncertainty understandable", "revisedQuote": "Its value lies in making this uncertainty understandable", "problem": "The revision removes the conditional qualification on the proposed study's value, presenting its benefit more definitively than the original supports."}]}], "sources": [{"id": "S1", "title": "Controlled source packet: domain and evidence brief", "excerpt": "The archaeological proposal uses dated charcoal fragments from a site. A fragment date estimates the age of sampled material, not necessarily the date of a building event. The reported interval is 1180 to 1260 CE. The relation between the charcoal and the building remains uncertain.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}, {"id": "S2", "title": "Controlled source packet: experimental design brief", "excerpt": "The team will compare 14 context descriptions. A cautious synthesis must preserve the full date interval and distinguish material age from event timing. Contexts with uncertain association will remain in the report. The study will not select the interval midpoint as an established construction date.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}]}
